Fault Tolerance vs High Availability — this is a very common interview topic, especially for SRE/Cloud roles.  

🔹 High Availability (HA)

A system designed to remain operational most of the time, even if some components fail.

⚙️ How it works
Uses redundancy
Detects failure and recovers quickly
May have brief interruption

🛠 Common Techniques
Load Balancer (e.g., AWS ELB)
Auto Scaling
Multi-AZ deployment
Health checks

====

🔹 Fault Tolerance (FT)

A system that continues to operate without any disruption, even when components fail.

⚙️ How it works
Uses real-time replication
No failover delay
Fully redundant components running simultaneously

🛠 Common Techniques
Active-Active architecture
Synchronous replication
Distributed systems with consensus
